---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { formatDate, listChapterIds, loadExternalLock, loadChapter, loadModelCoverage, shortCommit } from "../../lib/content";

const chapters = listChapterIds().map((id) => ({ id, ...loadChapter(id) }));
const { lock } = chapters[0];
const claimCount = chapters.reduce((n, c) => n + c.ledger.claims.length, 0);
const external = loadExternalLock();
const coverage = loadModelCoverage();
const awaitingReview = chapters.filter((c) => c.publication.reviewState === "draft-unreviewed").length;
// Excerpt descriptions in the lock's path field are labels, not GitHub paths.
const excerptPaths: Record<string, string[]> = {
  "core-script-assets-excerpt.json": ["unit_test_data/script_assets_test.json"],
  "core-locktime-cases-excerpt.json": ["src/test/data/tx_valid.json", "src/test/data/tx_invalid.json", "src/script/script.h"],
};
// Files the BIP text does not link itself (see each entry's note in the lock).
const citedLabel: Record<string, string> = {
  "core-locktime-cases-excerpt.json": "tests for the reference implementation linked by BIP",
};
---
<Base title="Methodology · BIP Atlas" description="Sources, checks and limits behind BIP Atlas." current="methodology">
  <div class="manual-page atlas-flow atlas-method">
    <h1>Methodology</h1>
    <p>
      Every chapter is built from a pinned revision of the <code>bitcoin/bips</code> repository. The current source is
      commit <a href={`https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/commit/${lock.commit}`}><code>{shortCommit(lock.commit)}</code></a>,
      read on {formatDate(lock.retrievedAt)}. A lock file records each file’s hash. Links in each chapter open the
      exact lines that support a statement.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some BIPs publish their test vectors in other repositories. Those files are fetched at an explicit commit and
      hashed too:
    </p>
    <ul>
      {external.files.map((f) => (
        <li>
          {(excerptPaths[f.file] ?? [f.path]).map((path, i) => <>{i > 0 && "; "}<a href={`${f.repository}/blob/${f.commit}/${path}`}>{f.repository.replace("https://github.com/", "")}/{path}</a></>)}
          {excerptPaths[f.file] && " (pinned excerpt)"} at <code>{shortCommit(f.commit)}</code>, {citedLabel[f.file] ?? "cited by BIP"} {f.citedBy.bip}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <h2>What has been checked</h2>
    <p>
      Every exact value in a figure comes from a tested model, computed at build time or in your browser. The
      models use <code>@noble</code> libraries for hashing, elliptic-curve arithmetic and ciphers. The block-filter
      model uses the <code>siphash</code> package for SipHash.
      The <a href="https://github.com/otaliptus/bip-atlas/tree/main/packages/models/test">model tests</a>
      and <a href="https://github.com/otaliptus/bip-atlas/tree/main/packages/figures/test">figure tests</a>
      compare published material with the implementation and add selected edge cases. The table lists what each
      model checks and where it stops. Passing these checks is narrower than full protocol conformance.
    </p>
    <div class="atlas-table-wrap atlas-coverage" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Model coverage by chapter">
      <table class="manual-table">
        <caption>Coverage and limits for all {chapters.length} chapters. On narrow screens, scroll the table horizontally to read every column.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Chapter</th><th scope="col">Published material</th><th scope="col">Additional checks</th><th scope="col">Limits and supplied values</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {chapters.map((c) => {
            const entry = coverage[c.id];
            return <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href={`/learn/${c.id}/`}>{entry.name}</a><br /><small>BIPs {c.publication.primaryBips.join(", ")}</small></th>
              <td>{entry.published}</td><td>{entry.additional}</td><td>{entry.limits}</td>
            </tr>;
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The {chapters.length} chapters make {claimCount} evidence claims. The build checks each supporting quote
      word for word at its cited source lines. It also checks that every paragraph cites a claim, that fixtures
      name their source, and that file hashes match. A matching quote shows what the source says. It does not
      prove that our own inference follows from it. Inferences are labelled in each chapter’s evidence list and
      still need review.
    </p>
    <h2>What has not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every chapter is hand-authored and has had one independent technical review. {awaitingReview} {awaitingReview === 1 ? "chapter was" : "chapters were"} revised afterwards and {awaitingReview === 1 ? "awaits" : "await"} a fresh review. None has formal sign-off yet.</li>
      <li>No automated writing pipeline is connected yet.</li>
      <li>The models are teaching models. They check structure and encodings against published vectors. They are not wallets, signers or full conformance suites. They say nothing about ownership, balance, or whether a payment is safe.</li>
      <li>No screen-reader session or accessibility audit has been performed beyond the checks recorded in the project.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Pages load no third-party scripts, fonts or analytics. Figures run entirely in your browser and never send
      what you do in them anywhere. They accept no typed addresses, keys, recovery phrases or PSBTs. Nothing on this
      site signs or broadcasts a transaction.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
